    "https://illinois.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/1/home/requisition/17941?c=illinois": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor- Anthropology",
      "description": "Assistant Professor- Anthropology | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) Assistant Professor- Anthropology Urbana, IL, United States | 1038184 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 9/9/2026 Back to Search Assistant Professor North American Archaeology College of Liberal Arts & Sciences University of Illinois Urbana-Champaign The Department of Anthropology at the University of Illinois Urbana-Champaign invites applications for a full-time, tenure-track Assistant Professor in Archaeology with a target start date of August 16, 2027. The successful candidate will contribute to the mission of the College of Liberal Arts & Sciences at the University of Illinois, where curiosity drives impact. As the heart of a leading land-grant research university, LAS brings together diverse disciplines to explore fundamental questions and address complex challenges. We prepare students for a lifetime of inquiry, leadership, and service through innovative research, transformative teaching, and thoughtful mentoring. We strongly encourage applications from those who have demonstrated the knowledge, skills, and experience needed to be effective teachers for our student population with its wide range of backgrounds and experiences, in alignment with the mission of our university. To learn more about the mission, vision, and values of the College of Liberal Arts & Sciences, visit: https://las.illinois.edu . Geographic area of research is North America with a preference for an archaeologist working in the Midwest US. Successful candidates will have a demonstrated commitment to Indigenous archaeology and ethical research. Candidates should provide evidence of engaging and collaborating with Indigenous groups and implementing NAGPRA (Native American Graves Protection and Repatriation Act) principles. Candidates also should identify plans for developing field or lab projects that train students and support research. Candidates will be expected to teach effectively at both the undergraduate and graduate levels, establish and maintain an active and independent archaeological research program that includes plans for peer-reviewed publications, and provide service to the department, the university, and the profession. PhD in anthropological archaeology, American Indian/Native American/Indigenous studies or a closely related field with a demonstrated specialty in archaeology required . Candidates whose PhD may be delayed but will complete all the Ph.D. requirements within the first appointment year may be appointed at the rank of Instructor. After the Ph.D. requirement is met, the appointment will be changed to Assistant Professor. Appointment Information The position is a full-time, 9-month, tenure-track faculty position at the assistant professor level, with an anticipated start date of August 16, 2027. The budgeted salary range for the position is $ $87,500-95,500 at the Assistant Professor level, for a 9-month service basis (paid over 12 months). The pay offered to the selected candidate will be determined based on factors including (but not limited to) the candidate's experience and qualifications, as well as equivalent years in rank, training, and field or discipline; internal equity; and external market pay for comparable jobs. It is not typical for a beginning Assistant Professor to be offered a salary at or near the top of the full range for the position. This position will be expected to work at the University of Illinois Urbana-Champaign campus on a full-time basis per the University’s Workplace Flexibility policy. This position is eligible for sponsorship for work authorization, except for sponsorship of a new H1B petition that would incur the $100,000 fee. Application Procedures & Deadline Information To apply, create your candidate profile through https://jobs.illinois.edu and submit application materials. Applicants should upload a letter of application, curriculum vitae, up to three publications, a research statement that includes experience with and plans for collaborations with tribes and a list of teaching interests and teaching experience, two sample syllabi, and contact information for three professional references. Letters of recommendation may be requested from referees at a later date. We ask that all documents be uploaded in a single .pdf file in the “Resume/CV” section. To ensure full consideration, applications should be received by 6pm (CST) on October 20, 2026 . Questions about the position may be directed to Professor Lisa J. Lucero at ljlucero@illinois.edu. Questions regarding the application materials may be directed to lascollegehiring@illinois.edu Questions regarding the application portal can be directed to 217-333-2137 or jobs@illinois.edu To find out more about the resources available at the university and Urbana-Champaign community please visit these sites: Benefits Dual Career Program Explore Champaign-Urbana Work-life balance and family-friendly programs The University of Illinois Urbana-Champaign (www.illinois.edu) is located approximately 120 miles south of Chicago in a metropolitan area of approximately 235,000 people. The campus is home to internationally recognized facilities and interdisciplinary programs including the Center for Indigenous Science (https://www.igb.illinois.edu/research/CIS), Carl R. Woese Institute for Genomic Biology (www.igb.illinois.edu), Beckman Institute (www.beckman.illinois.edu), Energy Biosciences Institute (http://energybiosciencesinstitute.org/), W.M. Keck Center for Comparative and Functional Genomics (www.biotech.uiuc.edu/centers/Keck), National Center for Supercomputing Applications (www.ncsa.illinois.edu), and the Institute for Sustainability, Energy, and Environment (https://sustainability.illinois.edu/). Founded in 1867 as Illinois’s flagship public university, the University of Illinois Urbana-Champaign empowers a global community of students, scholars, and alumni to change the world through bold, innovative research and transformative education. With a land-grant heritage rooted in progress, Illinois faculty drive paradigm-shifting discoveries, mentor future leaders, and collaborate across 15 colleges and instructional units and more than 20 research institutes. The university’s legacy of excellence includes 24 Nobel Prizes and 29 Pulitzer Prizes awarded to its faculty and alumni, $755 million in sponsored research funding, and 94 academic programs ranked in the top 20 nationally. Illinois offers the resources, recognition, and reach to accelerate your career — along with a highly competitive benefits portfolio. Discover how the Illinois Value Proposition fosters professional longevity, personal fulfillment, and a deep sense of purpose in every role. Faculty Recruitment Champaign-Urbana The \nUniversity of Illinois must also comply with applicable federal export \ncontrol laws and regulations and, as such, it reserves the right to \nemploy restricted party screening procedures for applicants. Artificial Intelligence (AI) tools may be used in some portions of the candidate review process for this position; however, all employment decisions will be made by a person. This position is intended to be eligible for benefits . This includes Health, Dental, Vision, Life Insurance, a Retirement Plan, Paid time Off, and Tuition waivers for employees and dependents. The University of Illinois System is an equal opportunity employer, including but not limited to disability and/or veteran status, and complies with all applicable state and federal employment mandates. Please visit Required Employment Notices and Posters to view our non-discrimination statement and find additional information about required background checks, sexual harassment/misconduct disclosures, and employment eligibility review through E-Verify . Applicants with disabilities are encouraged to apply and may request a reasonable accommodation under the Americans with Disabilities Act (2008) to complete the application and/or interview process. Accommodations may also be requested on the basis of pregnancy, childbirth, and related conditions, or religion. Requests may be submitted through the reasonable accommodation portal , or by contacting the Office for Access & Equity at 217-333-0885, option #1, or accessibility@illinois.edu . Requisition ID : 1038184 Job Category : Faculty Apply at: https://jobs.illinois.edu Apply Now Share Save Job Looking for more University of Illinois Positions? We invite you to search for positions at each of the University of Illinois' locations, the University of Illinois System Office and the University of Illinois Foundation. The University of Illinois System Office supports the primary missions of teaching, research, public service, and economic development for all of the Universities and offers positions in all locations. The University of Illinois Foundation is the official fundraising and private gift-receiving agency for the University of Illinois and also offers position in all locations.  Click the links below to search for other University of Illinois positions. University of Illinois Chicago University of Illinois Springfield University of Illinois System Office University of Illinois Foundation Illinois Human Resources University of Illinois Urbana-Champaign Personnel Services Building - MC 562 52 E. Gregory Dr. Champaign, IL  61820 217.333.2137 | jobs@illinois.edu humanresources.illinois.edu"
    },
    "https://illinois.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/1/home/requisition/17845?c=illinois": {
      "title": "Assistant / Associate / Full Professor Land Use (Tenure-Track) - Urban & Regional Planning",
      "description": "Assistant / Associate / Full Professor Land Use (Tenure-Track) - Urban & Regional Planning | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) Assistant / Associate / Full Professor Land Use (Tenure-Track) - Urban & Regional Planning Urbana, IL, United States | 1038126 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 9/8/2026 Back to Search Assistant Professor/Associate Professor/Professor - Land Use (Tenure-Track) Department of Urban and Regional Planning College of Fine & Applied Arts University of Illinois Urbana-Champaign The Department of Urban and Regional Planning at the University of Illinois\nUrbana-Champaign is searching for a full-time Assistant Professor/Associate\nProfessor/Professor with expertise in land-use and environmental planning. Candidates\nwhose expertise includes local and regional governance, sustainability and\nclimate, or ecology are particularly encouraged to apply. We are open to\nscholars who employ a range of innovative methods, ranging from data science\nand analytics to ethnography, to community-engaged research and decolonial\napproaches. While we prefer that candidates research and teaching engage\nquestions of land use and environment in the U.S., we welcome those whose work incorporates\na comparative or transnational perspective. Planning at Illinois seeks answers to today’s biggest social\nchallenges through creative, multidisciplinary, and community-driven solutions.\nWe live our university’s land grant mission while pursuing global impact and\nprepare practitioners and researchers to lead in the development of novel\napproaches to just, sustainable urban environments. The campus and the\nDepartment provide ample support for faculty to conduct interdisciplinary\nresearch and innovative teaching. Members of the DURP faculty are involved in a\nbroad array of ongoing research and public engagement activities throughout\nIllinois, the U.S., and internationally.  DURP faculty contribute\ncourses to the Department’s three degree programs: Bachelor of Arts in Urban\nStudies and Planning (BAUSP), Master of Urban Planning (MUP), and Regional\nPlanning Ph.D. The College of Fine and Applied Arts (FAA) is singular in the nation for its diversity, innovation and breadth. Its mission is dedicated to the advancement,\npractice, and understanding of the arts,\nand its central focus is the synergy between research and the preparation of students for professional careers in the\ncreation and interpretation of\nthe environmental, visual, and performing arts. Deeply related to that focus is the commitment to elevate and\nsustain the study of the arts as\nboth a necessary mode of understanding and a vibrant expression of human experience within the local,\nnational, and international\ncommunities. The college comprises the Schools of Music , Architecture , and Art and Design ; Departments of Dance , Landscape Architecture , Theatre , and Urban and Regional Planning ;\nthe Sustainable Design program; Krannert Center for the Performing Arts ; Krannert Art Museum ; and Japan House . FAA\nemploys more than 660 faculty members\nand staff, including more than 150 tenure system faculty members, and more than 1,850 undergraduate and 635 graduate\nstudents enroll in FAA’s more\nthan 30 majors and 10 minors. Qualifications Required – Assessment of\napplications will focus on expertise fitting the position description; research\nprogram; and approach to teaching research and engagement. Applicants at the Assistant\nProfessor level must have a promising research agenda and a strong commitment\nto undergraduate and graduate teaching. Applicants at the Associate or Full\nlevel must have a demonstrated record of excellence in research, teaching, and\nservice. A Ph.D. in planning or related fields is required - ABD applicants who\nexpect to complete their Ph.D. prior to the position start date are welcome to\napply. Preferred – Contribution of service to the field. Social justice dimensions are a key component of our program\nofferings. To increase this profile, we strongly encourage applications from\nindividuals with demonstrable commitments to equity and social justice through\nteaching, research, and/or community engagement, and a reflective approach to\ntransforming the discipline with respect to inclusion and anti-racism. We\nencourage applications from candidates of all backgrounds who bring experience\nworking with under-represented and underserved communities and traditions. Salary and Appointment Information This is a nine-month faculty appointment (paid over 12\nmonths). The anticipated start date is August 16, 2027. The budgeted salary range for the position is $76,000 to $85,000\nat the Assistant Professor level, $91,000 to $110,000 at the Associate\nProfessor level, and $115,000 to $135,000 at the Full Professor level. We\nstrive to provide a competitive salary, considering factors such as available\nmarket data, internal equity, candidate’s experience and qualifications, and\nbudget constraints. This position is eligible for\nsponsorship for work authorization, except for sponsorship of a new H1B\npetition that would incur the $100,000 fee. Application Procedures and Deadline Information Applications must be received by October 16, 2026 at 6:00pm CST .\nApply for this position using the “Apply Now” button in the job posting at\nhttp://jobs.illinois.edu and upload the following items: • CV/Resume • Cover Letter Applications not submitted through http://jobs.illinois.edu\nwill not be considered. For further information about this specific position,\nplease contact FAA HR at faa-hr@illinois.edu . For questions regarding the\napplication process, please contact 217-333-2137. Founded in 1867 as Illinois’s flagship public university, the University of Illinois Urbana-Champaign empowers a global community of students, scholars, and alumni to change the world through bold, innovative research and transformative education. With a land-grant heritage rooted in progress, Illinois faculty drive paradigm-shifting discoveries, mentor future leaders, and collaborate across 15 colleges and instructional units and more than 20 research institutes. The university’s legacy of excellence includes 24 Nobel Prizes and 29 Pulitzer Prizes awarded to its faculty and alumni, $755 million in sponsored research funding, and 94 academic programs ranked in the top 20 nationally. Illinois offers the resources, recognition, and reach to accelerate your career — along with a highly competitive benefits portfolio. Discover how the Illinois Value Proposition fosters professional longevity, personal fulfillment, and a deep sense of purpose in every role. Faculty Recruitment Champaign-Urbana Artificial Intelligence (AI) tools may be used in some portions of the candidate review process for this position; however, all employment decisions will be made by a person. This position is intended to be eligible for benefits . This includes Health, Dental, Vision, Life Insurance, a Retirement Plan, Paid time Off, and Tuition waivers for employees and dependents. The University of Illinois System is an equal opportunity employer, including but not limited to disability and/or veteran status, and complies with all applicable state and federal employment mandates. Please visit Required Employment Notices and Posters to view our non-discrimination statement and find additional information about required background checks, sexual harassment/misconduct disclosures, and employment eligibility review through E-Verify . Applicants with disabilities are encouraged to apply and may request a reasonable accommodation under the Americans with Disabilities Act (2008) to complete the application and/or interview process. Accommodations may also be requested on the basis of pregnancy, childbirth, and related conditions, or religion. Requests may be submitted through the reasonable accommodation portal , or by contacting the Office for Access & Equity at 217-333-0885, option #1, or accessibility@illinois.edu . Requisition ID : 1038126 Job Category : Faculty Apply at: https://jobs.illinois.edu Apply Now Share Save Job Looking for more University of Illinois Positions? We invite you to search for positions at each of the University of Illinois' locations, the University of Illinois System Office and the University of Illinois Foundation. The University of Illinois System Office supports the primary missions of teaching, research, public service, and economic development for all of the Universities and offers positions in all locations. The University of Illinois Foundation is the official fundraising and private gift-receiving agency for the University of Illinois and also offers position in all locations.  Click the links below to search for other University of Illinois positions. University of Illinois Chicago University of Illinois Springfield University of Illinois System Office University of Illinois Foundation Illinois Human Resources University of Illinois Urbana-Champaign Personnel Services Building - MC 562 52 E. Gregory Dr. Champaign, IL  61820 217.333.2137 | jobs@illinois.edu humanresources.illinois.edu"
    },
    "https://illinois.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/1/home/requisition/16661?c=illinois": {
      "title": "Grainger Engineering: Teaching Professor (Open Rank) - Landuyt Center for Entrepreneurship, ILEE",
      "description": "Grainger Engineering: Teaching Professor (Open Rank) - Landuyt Center for Entrepreneurship, ILEE | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) Grainger Engineering: Teaching Professor (Open Rank) - Landuyt Center for Entrepreneurship, ILEE Urbana, IL, United States | 1035886 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 8/27/2026 Back to Search Teaching Professor (Open Rank) Landuyt Center for Entrepreneurship Innovation, Leadership, and Engineering Entrepreneurship Grainger College of Engineering University of Illinois Urbana-Champaign The Landuyt Center for Entrepreneurship in The Grainger College of Engineering at the University of Illinois Urbana-Champaign invites applications for an open-rank, full-time teaching faculty position at the assistant, associate, or full professor rank, in the Innovation, Leadership, and Engineering Entrepreneurship Program. We seek applicants with a strong commitment to excellence in teaching by delivering high-impact engineering entrepreneurship education and experiential programming to students of all levels. This is a 100% non-tenure track, career-oriented, renewable appointment. This position joins the Landuyt Center for Entrepreneurship at a period of transformational growth and strategic expansion, providing an opportunity to shape the future of innovation and entrepreneurial education at Illinois. The candidate will support rising engagement by teaching existing courses and developing new, high-impact educational opportunities that integrate theory and application. In addition to for-credit courses, candidates may contribute to instructional efforts through co-curricular programming, such as the Cozad New Venture Challenge. This position will also mentor student teams to expand venture creation efforts, contribute to broadening entrepreneurial mindset development across campus, and participate in research-oriented entrepreneurial education projects and disseminate findings to campus and external audiences. The ideal candidate will have expertise in generative AI to develop next-generation entrepreneurial learning experiences and instructional approaches. This position will engage with campus partners throughout the entrepreneurial ecosystem at Illinois.  Candidates will also have opportunities to interact with a large community of engineering education researchers through the Academy for Excellence in Engineering Education (AE3) and Center for Innovation in Teaching and Learning (CITL). A doctoral degree in engineering or related field is required at the start date, as well as demonstrated interest or experience in technology commercialization, deep-tech venture creation, customer discovery, innovation, and creativity. Successful candidates will have knowledge of effective, evidence-based pedagogical practices, experience in developing curriculum, and a demonstrated ability to effectively teach and mentor/advise students from a wide range of disciplines at both the undergraduate and graduate level. In addition to teaching efforts, this position also has the opportunity to engage in research and service activities at the unit, college, and/or campus level. The budgeted salary range for the position is $90,000 to $97,000 at the Teaching Assistant Professor level, $97,000 to $105,000 at the Teaching Associate Professor level, and $105,000 to $115,000 at the Teaching Professor level, for a 9-month service basis paid over 12 months. Salary is competitive and commensurate with qualifications and experience, while also considering internal equity.  This position is eligible for work authorization sponsorship. Full consideration will be given to applications received by October 18, 2026. Applications may be reviewed as they are received. Those submitted after the stated deadline may still be considered until the position is filled. Applicants may be interviewed before the closing date; however, no hiring decision will be made until after that date. A start date is expected in the spring of 2027; however, this is negotiable. To apply for this position, please create a candidate profile at https://jobs.illinois.edu. The application package should include the following materials uploaded as a single PDF file in the “Resume/CV” section: 1) cover letter, 2) curriculum vitae, 3) teaching statement, 4) service statement, 5) research statement, and 6) names and contact information for three professional references (no letters required at this time). The teaching, service, and research statements offer a chance to share your motivation, approach, experience, leadership, impact, and vision in each area, including how you would support the university’s land-grant mission ( https://boldly.illinois.edu/ ), through campus, community, or professional engagement. For further information regarding application procedures, please address questions to Dawn Creath at dcreath@illinois.edu . We have an active and successful Dual Career Academic Couples Program and a strong commitment to work-life balance and family-friendly programs for faculty and staff ( https://provost.illinois.edu/faculty-affairs/work-life-balance/ ). Founded in 1867 as Illinois’s flagship public university, the University of Illinois Urbana-Champaign empowers a global community of students, scholars, and alumni to change the world through bold, innovative research and transformative education. With a land-grant heritage rooted in progress, Illinois faculty drive paradigm-shifting discoveries, mentor future leaders, and collaborate across 15 colleges and instructional units and more than 20 research institutes. The university’s legacy of excellence includes 24 Nobel Prizes and 29 Pulitzer Prizes awarded to its faculty and alumni, $755 million in sponsored research funding, and 94 academic programs ranked in the top 20 nationally. Illinois offers resources, recognition, and reach to accelerate your career — along with a highly competitive benefits portfolio. Discover how the Illinois Value Proposition fosters professional longevity, personal fulfillment, and a deep sense of purpose in every role. Faculty Recruitment Champaign-Urbana Artificial Intelligence (AI) tools may be used in some portions of the candidate review process for this position; however, all employment decisions will be made by a person. This position is intended to be eligible for benefits . This includes health, dental, vision, life insurance, a retirement plan, paid time off, and tuition waivers for employees and dependents. The University of Illinois must also comply with applicable federal export control laws and regulations and, as such, reserves the right to employ restricted party screening procedures for applicants. The University of Illinois System is an equal opportunity employer, including but not limited to disability and/or veteran status, and complies with all applicable state and federal employment mandates. Please visit Required Employment Notices and Posters to view our non-discrimination statement and find additional information about required background checks, sexual harassment/misconduct disclosures, and employment eligibility review through E-Verify . Applicants with disabilities are encouraged to apply and may request a reasonable accommodation under the Americans with Disabilities Act (2008) to complete the application and/or interview process. Accommodations may also be requested on the basis of pregnancy, childbirth, and related conditions, or religion. Requests may be submitted through the reasonable accommodation portal , or by contacting the Office for Access & Equity at 217-333-0885, option #1, or accessibility@illinois.edu . Requisition ID : 1035886 Job Category : Faculty Apply at: https://jobs.illinois.edu Apply Now Share Save Job Looking for more University of Illinois Positions? We invite you to search for positions at each of the University of Illinois' locations, the University of Illinois System Office and the University of Illinois Foundation. The University of Illinois System Office supports the primary missions of teaching, research, public service, and economic development for all of the Universities and offers positions in all locations. The University of Illinois Foundation is the official fundraising and private gift-receiving agency for the University of Illinois and also offers position in all locations.  Click the links below to search for other University of Illinois positions. University of Illinois Chicago University of Illinois Springfield University of Illinois System Office University of Illinois Foundation Illinois Human Resources University of Illinois Urbana-Champaign Personnel Services Building - MC 562 52 E. Gregory Dr. Champaign, IL  61820 217.333.2137 | jobs@illinois.edu humanresources.illinois.edu"
    },
    "https://illinois.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/1/home/requisition/17578?c=illinois": {
      "title": "Assistant/Associate/Full Professor- Chemical & Biomolecular Engineering",
      "description": "Assistant/Associate/Full Professor- Chemical & Biomolecular Engineering | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) Assistant/Associate/Full Professor- Chemical & Biomolecular Engineering Urbana, IL, United States | 1037104 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 8/20/2026 Back to Search UNIVERSITY OF ILLINOIS URBANA-CHAMPAIGN CHEMICAL AND BIOMOLECULAR ENGINEERING FACULTY POSITION The Department of Chemical and Biomolecular Engineering at the University of Illinois at Urbana-Champaign seeks candidates for a full-time faculty position. Applications are welcome for tenure-track or tenured faculty positions at the Assistant, Associate, or Full Professor level in all areas of chemical and biomolecular engineering. Areas of particular interest include AI/ML, biomolecular engineering, chemical separations, clean energy and sustainability, and process systems engineering. Faculty members are expected to initiate and sustain a vigorous research program, teach undergraduate and graduate students, and support the administrative and governance functions of the department, the university, and the profession through service on committees, as appropriate. The successful candidate will contribute to the mission of the College of Liberal Arts & Sciences (LAS) at the University of Illinois, where curiosity drives impact. As the heart of a leading land-grant research university, LAS brings together diverse disciplines to explore fundamental questions and address complex challenges. We prepare students for a lifetime of inquiry, leadership, and service through innovative research, transformative teaching, and thoughtful mentoring. We strongly encourage applications from those who have demonstrated the knowledge, skills, and experience needed to be effective teachers for our student population, with its wide range of backgrounds and experiences, in alignment with our university's mission. To learn more about the mission, vision, and values of the College of Liberal Arts & Sciences, visit: https://las.illinois.edu . Qualifications An earned Ph.D. in chemical engineering, materials science, chemistry, mechanical engineering, bioengineering, biomedical engineering, applied math, biotechnology, chemical technology, or a related field with a distinguished academic record is required. Applicants at the assistant professor level must have a promising research agenda and a commitment to undergraduate and graduate teaching. Applicants at the Associate or Full Professor level must demonstrate a record of research, teaching, and service indicative of an Associate or Full Professor. Appointment Information The target starting date is August 16, 2027, but is flexible based on the candidate’s needs.  The budgeted salary range for the position is $115,000 to $135,000 at the Assistant Professor level, $135,000 to $160,000 at the Associate Professor level, and $160,000 to $220,000 at the Full Professor level, for a 9-month service basis (paid over 12 months). The pay offered to the selected candidate will be determined based on factors including (but not limited to) the experience and qualifications of the selected candidate, including equivalent years in rank, training, and field or discipline; internal equity; and external market pay for comparable jobs. It is not typical for a beginning Assistant Professor to be offered a salary at or near the top of the full range for the position. This position will be expected to work at the University of Illinois Urbana-Champaign campus on a full-time basis per the University’s Workplace Flexibility policy. This position is eligible for sponsorship for work authorization. To find out more about the resources available at the university and Urbana-Champaign community, please visit these sites: Benefits Dual Career Program Explore Champaign-Urbana Work-life balance and family-friendly programs Application Procedures & Deadline Information For full consideration, applications must be received by 6 pm (CST) on November 20, 2026 . To apply, visit http://go.illinois.edu/CHBEfaculty and submit: (1) Cover letter (2) Curriculum vitae (3) Names and contact information of at least three professional references (4) Description of prior research accomplishments (2 pages) (5) Statement of future research program directions (3 pages) (6) Statement of teaching philosophy (1 page) Applicants will be evaluated solely on the materials submitted and should provide clear, specific evidence of their qualifications. Application materials must first demonstrate a strong record of research and scholarly achievement, including research accomplishments, future research goals, and the potential impact of the applicant’s work. Materials must also demonstrate a commitment to excellence in student-centered teaching and mentoring. We request that all documents be uploaded as a single .pdf file in the “Resume/CV” section. Questions about the position can be addressed to the Chemical and Biomolecular Engineering department office, 217-244-9214, chbe_apply@scs.uiuc.edu . For questions regarding the application portal, please contact 217-333-2137 or jobs@illinois.edu . Founded in 1867 as Illinois’s flagship public university, the University of Illinois Urbana-Champaign empowers a global community of students, scholars, and alumni to change the world through bold, innovative research and transformative education. With a land-grant heritage rooted in progress, Illinois faculty drive paradigm-shifting discoveries, mentor future leaders, and collaborate across 15 colleges and instructional units and more than 20 research institutes. The university’s legacy of excellence includes 24 Nobel Prizes and 29 Pulitzer Prizes awarded to its faculty and alumni, $755 million in sponsored research funding, and 94 academic programs ranked in the top 20 nationally. Illinois offers the resources, recognition, and reach to accelerate your career — along with a highly competitive benefits portfolio. Discover how the Illinois Value Proposition fosters professional longevity, personal fulfillment, and a deep sense of purpose in every role. Faculty Recruitment The\nUniversity of Illinois must also comply with applicable federal export control\nlaws and regulations and, as such, reserves the right to employ restricted\nparty screening procedures for applicants. Artificial Intelligence (AI) tools may be used in some portions of the candidate review process for this position; however, all employment decisions will be made by a person. This position is intended to be eligible for benefits . This includes Health, Dental, Vision, Life Insurance, a Retirement Plan, Paid time Off, and Tuition waivers for employees and dependents. The University of Illinois System is an equal opportunity employer, including but not limited to disability and/or veteran status, and complies with all applicable state and federal employment mandates. Please visit Required Employment Notices and Posters to view our non-discrimination statement and find additional information about required background checks, sexual harassment/misconduct disclosures, and employment eligibility review through E-Verify . Applicants with disabilities are encouraged to apply and may request a reasonable accommodation under the Americans with Disabilities Act (2008) to complete the application and/or interview process. Accommodations may also be requested on the basis of pregnancy, childbirth, and related conditions, or religion. Requests may be submitted through the reasonable accommodation portal , or by contacting the Office for Access & Equity at 217-333-0885, option #1, or accessibility@illinois.edu . Requisition ID : 1037104 Job Category : Faculty Apply at: https://jobs.illinois.edu Apply Now Share Save Job Looking for more University of Illinois Positions? We invite you to search for positions at each of the University of Illinois' locations, the University of Illinois System Office and the University of Illinois Foundation. The University of Illinois System Office supports the primary missions of teaching, research, public service, and economic development for all of the Universities and offers positions in all locations. The University of Illinois Foundation is the official fundraising and private gift-receiving agency for the University of Illinois and also offers position in all locations.  Click the links below to search for other University of Illinois positions. University of Illinois Chicago University of Illinois Springfield University of Illinois System Office University of Illinois Foundation Illinois Human Resources University of Illinois Urbana-Champaign Personnel Services Building - MC 562 52 E. Gregory Dr. Champaign, IL  61820 217.333.2137 | jobs@illinois.edu humanresources.illinois.edu"
