    "https://illinois.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/1/home/requisition/17567?c=illinois": {
      "title": "Assistant/Associate Professor- Microbiology",
      "description": "Assistant/Associate Professor- Microbiology | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) Assistant/Associate Professor- Microbiology Urbana, IL, United States | 1037112 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 8/12/2026 Back to Search Assistant or Associate Professor Department of Microbiology School of Molecular and Cellular Biology College of Liberal Arts & Sciences University of Illinois at Urbana-Champaign The Department of Microbiology in the School of Molecular and Cellular Biology ( https://mcb.illinois.edu/departments/microbiology/ ) at the University of Illinois at Urbana-Champaign seeks applicants for a full-time tenure track position at the Assistant or Associate Professor level. Candidates who will enhance and expand the department’s strengths in exploring the fundamental biology of microbes and their viruses are encouraged to apply. The ideal candidate will bridge classical microbiology with advanced experimental and computational approaches to investigate the basic biology, physiology, ecology, and evolution of Bacteria, Archaea, and their viruses. The investigations will integrate knowledge and principles of physiology, structure-function relationships, metabolism, and genetic mechanisms to elucidate how microbes interact with their environments, ranging from the broader environment to host-pathogen interactions. The candidate is expected to conduct independent research, participate in our B.S. and Ph.D. programs, teach effectively at the undergraduate and graduate levels, and provide service to the department, the university and the profession. Microbial research at the University of Illinois has contributed foundational insights into microbial physiology, evolution, ecology, pathogenesis, and genetics. Successful candidates will hold an appointment in the Department of Microbiology within the School of Molecular and Cellular Biology. The department also leads the campus-wide Microbial Systems Initiative (https://msi.research.illinois.edu), which brings together scientists from over fifty campus units with the aim of promoting collaboration and supporting large-scale research efforts. Interdisciplinary research institutes, including the Carl R. Woese Institute for Genomic Biology (IGB –https://igb.illinois.edu), the Beckman Institute for Advanced Science and Technology (https://beckman.illinois.edu), and the National Center for Supercomputing Applications (https://ncsa.illinois.edu) support collaborative team science research. The IGB is home to multi-investigator research themes studying microbiomes in health and disease, infectious disease genomics, antimicrobial resistance, antimicrobial discovery, and One Health. The Roy J. Carver Center for Biotechnology (https://biotech.illinois.edu) offers easy and affordable access to world-class core facilities including next-generation sequencing, microscopy, flow cytometry, and proteomics. Successful candidates will be part of a large cohort of faculty contributing to and benefitting from this rich microbial-systems research environment. The successful candidate will contribute to the mission of the College of Liberal Arts & Sciences at the University of Illinois, where curiosity drives impact. As the heart of a leading land-grant research university, LAS brings together diverse disciplines to explore fundamental questions and address complex challenges. We prepare students for a lifetime of inquiry, leadership, and service through innovative research, transformative teaching, and thoughtful mentoring. We strongly encourage applications from those who have demonstrated the knowledge, skills, and experience needed to be effective teachers for our student population with its wide range of backgrounds and experiences, in alignment with the mission of our university. To learn more about the mission, vision, and values of the College of Liberal Arts & Sciences, visit: https://las.illinois.edu . Candidates must hold a Ph.D. in microbiology or a related field, have postdoctoral experience, have a track record of creativity and productivity, show evidence or promise of developing a record of teaching effectiveness, and exhibit potential for independent research. The target starting date is August 16, 2027. The budgeted 9-month salary range for the position is $90,000-$95,000 at the Assistant Professor level and $105-$120,000 at the Associate Professor level (paid over 12 months). The pay offered to the selected candidate will be determined based on factors including (but not limited to) the experience and qualifications of the selected candidate, including equivalent years in rank, training, and field or discipline; internal equity; and external market pay for comparable jobs. The 9-month salary can be supplemented with summer salary by startup or external funds. Startup packages are highly competitive. This position will be expected to work at the University of Illinois Urbana-Champaign campus on a full-time basis per the University’s Workplace Flexibility policy. This position is eligible for sponsorship for work authorization, except for sponsorship of a new H1B petition that would incur the $100,000 fee. This position is intended to be eligible for benefits . These include Health, Dental, Vision, Life Insurance, a Retirement Plan, and Tuition waivers for employees and dependents. To apply, create your candidate profile and submit application materials at https://jobs.illinois.edu . Required materials include the following: cover letter addressing how the applicant meets the required and preferred qualifications for the position curriculum vitae concise summary of past research accomplishments (2 pages or less) statement of future research plans (2 pages or less) teaching statement addressing experience, approach to teaching, and topics of interest (2 pages or less) We ask that the above documents be uploaded as a single pdf file in the “Resume/CV” section. An email request for contact information for three professional references will be sent to you 1-2 business days after your application is submitted. Once the contact information for the references is uploaded into the system, their letters will be invited. Early application submission is encouraged to allow time for referees to submit letters of recommendation. For full consideration, the information above should be submitted by 6 pm CST on October 30, 2026 . Although early applications are appreciated and interviews may be conducted before the closing date, hiring decisions will not be made until after the closing date. Questions can be addressed to hr@mcb.illinois.edu. For questions regarding the application portal, please contact 217-333-2137 or jobs@illinois.edu. Founded in 1867 as Illinois’s flagship public university, the University of Illinois Urbana-Champaign empowers a global community of students, scholars, and alumni to change the world through bold, innovative research and transformative education. With a land-grant heritage rooted in progress, Illinois faculty drive paradigm-shifting discoveries, mentor future leaders, and collaborate across 15 colleges and instructional units and more than 20 research institutes. The university’s legacy of excellence includes 24 Nobel Prizes and 29 Pulitzer Prizes awarded to its faculty and alumni, $755 million in sponsored research funding, and 94 academic programs ranked in the top 20 nationally. Illinois offers the resources, recognition, and reach to accelerate your career — along with a highly competitive benefits portfolio. Discover how the Illinois Value Proposition fosters professional longevity, personal fulfillment, and a deep sense of purpose in every role. To find out more about the resources available at the University and Urbana-Champaign community, please visit these sites: Dual Career Program Benefits Explore Champaign-Urbana Work-Life Balance & Family Friendly Programs Faculty Recruitment The University of Illinois must also comply with applicable federal export control laws and regulations and, as such, reserves the right to employ restricted party screening procedures for applicants. Artificial Intelligence (AI) tools may be used in some portions of the candidate review process for this position; however, all employment decisions will be made by a person. This position is intended to be eligible for benefits . This includes Health, Dental, Vision, Life Insurance, a Retirement Plan, Paid time Off, and Tuition waivers for employees and dependents. The University of Illinois System is an equal opportunity employer, including but not limited to disability and/or veteran status, and complies with all applicable state and federal employment mandates. Please visit Required Employment Notices and Posters to view our non-discrimination statement and find additional information about required background checks, sexual harassment/misconduct disclosures, and employment eligibility review through E-Verify . Applicants with disabilities are encouraged to apply and may request a reasonable accommodation under the Americans with Disabilities Act (2008) to complete the application and/or interview process. Accommodations may also be requested on the basis of pregnancy, childbirth, and related conditions, or religion. Requests may be submitted through the reasonable accommodation portal , or by contacting the Office for Access & Equity at 217-333-0885, option #1, or accessibility@illinois.edu . Requisition ID : 1037112 Job Category : Faculty Apply at: https://jobs.illinois.edu Apply Now Share Save Job Looking for more University of Illinois Positions? We invite you to search for positions at each of the University of Illinois' locations, the University of Illinois System Office and the University of Illinois Foundation. The University of Illinois System Office supports the primary missions of teaching, research, public service, and economic development for all of the Universities and offers positions in all locations. The University of Illinois Foundation is the official fundraising and private gift-receiving agency for the University of Illinois and also offers position in all locations.  Click the links below to search for other University of Illinois positions. University of Illinois Chicago University of Illinois Springfield University of Illinois System Office University of Illinois Foundation Illinois Human Resources University of Illinois Urbana-Champaign Personnel Services Building - MC 562 52 E. Gregory Dr. Champaign, IL  61820 217.333.2137 | jobs@illinois.edu humanresources.illinois.edu"
    },
    "https://illinois.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/1/home/requisition/17563?c=illinois": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor- Entomology",
      "description": "Assistant Professor- Entomology | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) Assistant Professor- Entomology Urbana, IL, United States | 1037109 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 8/12/2026 Back to Search Assistant Professor Insect Declines College of Liberal Arts & Sciences University of Illinois Urbana-Champaign The Department of Entomology and the School of Integrative Biology at the University of Illinois at Urbana-Champaign invite applications from entomologists with research portfolios in which insect biodiversity loss is a key element, including understanding how anthropogenic stressors (such as land-use change, climate change, agriculture, invasive species, and pollution) are causing declines in insect abundance, biomass, species richness, or range size. Candidates whose work addresses amelioration of anthropogenic changes to species, populations, and people, and who are working to develop new strategies for insect and biodiversity conservation and long-term monitoring, are especially welcome to apply. We additionally encourage researchers who can build connections and expand research in understudied global regions. The successful candidate will contribute to the mission of the College of Liberal Arts & Sciences at the University of Illinois, where curiosity drives impact. As the heart of a leading land-grant research university, LAS brings together diverse disciplines to explore fundamental questions and address complex challenges. We prepare students for a lifetime of inquiry, leadership, and service through innovative research, transformative teaching, and thoughtful mentoring. We strongly encourage applications from those who have demonstrated the knowledge, skills, and experience needed to be effective teachers for our student population with its wide range of backgrounds and experiences, in alignment with the mission of our university. To learn more about the mission, vision, and values of the College of Liberal Arts & Sciences, visit: https://las.illinois.edu . The position is a full-time, 9-month, tenure-track faculty position at the assistant professor level, with an anticipated start date of August 16, 2027. The successful candidate is expected to develop an externally funded research program and collaborate to develop research initiatives; this position provides an opportunity to join a dynamic and well-established community of biologists with interests spanning a wide range of taxa in the School of Integrative Biology, as well as many interdisciplinary programs across the campus, including the Illinois Natural History Survey, which houses several large invertebrate collections, the Carl R. Woese Institute for Genomic Biology, and the Beckman Institute for Science and Technology. Responsibilities also include undergraduate and/or graduate teaching (to be determined based on departmental need and candidate strengths), participation in both undergraduate and graduate training, and to provide service to the department, the university and the profession. Qualifications The successful candidate must have a Ph.D. in entomology, ecology, evolution, biology, zoology, genetics/genomics, conservation biology, or a related discipline. Applicants must show evidence of research productivity and evidence (or promise of developing) teaching and mentorship effectiveness at the undergraduate and graduate levels. Candidates whose PhD may be delayed but will complete all the Ph.D. requirements within the first appointment year may be appointed at the rank of Instructor. After the Ph.D. requirement is met, the appointment will be changed to Assistant Professor. Appointment Information The budgeted salary range for the position is $91,800 to $98,000 at the Assistant Professor level, for a 9-month service basis ( paid over 12 months). The pay offered to the selected candidate will be determined based on factors, including (but not limited to) the candidate's experience and qualifications, as well as equivalent years in rank, training, and field or discipline; internal equity; and external market pay for comparable jobs. It is not typical for a beginning Assistant Professor to be offered a salary at or near the top of the full range for the position. This position will be expected to work at the University of Illinois Urbana-Champaign campus on a full-time basis per the University’s Workplace Flexibility policy. This position is eligible for sponsorship for work authorization, except for sponsorship of a new H1B petition that would incur the $100,000 fee. Application Procedures & Deadline Information To apply, create your candidate profile through https://jobs.illinois.edu and submit application materials. Applicants should upload a letter of application addressing how they meet the qualifications for the position, curriculum vitae, links to 3 representative publications, a statement of teaching philosophy and interests, a statement of research interests, and contact information for three professional references. We ask that all documents be uploaded in a single .pdf file in the “Resume/CV” section. Applications submitted through the University of Illinois Job Board will be considered. To ensure full consideration, applications should be received by 6pm (CST) on October 1, 2026 . Interviews may take place before the closing date; however, no hiring decision will be made until after that date. Questions about the position may be directed to Kim Leigh at kaleigh@illinois.edu. Questions regarding the application materials may be directed to lascollegehiring@illinois.edu Questions regarding the application portal can be directed to 217-333-2137 or jobs@illinois.edu To find out more about the resources available at the university and Urbana-Champaign community please visit these sites: Benefits Dual Career Program Explore Champaign-Urbana Work-life balance and family-friendly programs The University of Illinois Urbana-Champaign (www.illinois.edu) is located approximately 120 miles south of Chicago in a metropolitan area of approximately 235,000 people. The campus is home to internationally recognized facilities and interdisciplinary programs including the Carl R. Woese Institute for Genomic Biology (www.igb.illinois.edu), Beckman Institute (www.beckman.illinois.edu), Energy Biosciences Institute (http://energybiosciencesinstitute.org/), W.M. Keck Center for Comparative and Functional Genomics (www.biotech.uiuc.edu/centers/Keck), National Center for Supercomputing Applications (www.ncsa.illinois.edu), and the Institute for Sustainability, Energy, and Environment (https://sustainability.illinois.edu/). The University of Illinois must also comply with applicable federal export control laws and regulations and, as such, it reserves the right to employ restricted party screening procedures for applicants. Founded in 1867 as Illinois’s flagship public university, the University of Illinois Urbana-Champaign empowers a global community of students, scholars, and alumni to change the world through bold, innovative research and transformative education. With a land-grant heritage rooted in progress, Illinois faculty drive paradigm-shifting discoveries, mentor future leaders, and collaborate across 15 colleges and instructional units and more than 20 research institutes. The university’s legacy of excellence includes 24 Nobel Prizes and 29 Pulitzer Prizes awarded to its faculty and alumni, $755 million in sponsored research funding, and 94 academic programs ranked in the top 20 nationally. Illinois offers the resources, recognition, and reach to accelerate your career — along with a highly competitive benefits portfolio. Discover how the Illinois Value Proposition fosters professional longevity, personal fulfillment, and a deep sense of purpose in every role. Faculty Recruitment Champaign-Urbana Artificial Intelligence (AI) tools may be used in some portions of the candidate review process for this position; however, all employment decisions will be made by a person. This position is intended to be eligible for benefits . This includes Health, Dental, Vision, Life Insurance, a Retirement Plan, Paid time Off, and Tuition waivers for employees and dependents. The University of Illinois System is an equal opportunity employer, including but not limited to disability and/or veteran status, and complies with all applicable state and federal employment mandates. Please visit Required Employment Notices and Posters to view our non-discrimination statement and find additional information about required background checks, sexual harassment/misconduct disclosures, and employment eligibility review through E-Verify . Applicants with disabilities are encouraged to apply and may request a reasonable accommodation under the Americans with Disabilities Act (2008) to complete the application and/or interview process. Accommodations may also be requested on the basis of pregnancy, childbirth, and related conditions, or religion. Requests may be submitted through the reasonable accommodation portal , or by contacting the Office for Access & Equity at 217-333-0885, option #1, or accessibility@illinois.edu . Requisition ID : 1037109 Job Category : Faculty Apply at: https://jobs.illinois.edu Apply Now Share Save Job Looking for more University of Illinois Positions? We invite you to search for positions at each of the University of Illinois' locations, the University of Illinois System Office and the University of Illinois Foundation. The University of Illinois System Office supports the primary missions of teaching, research, public service, and economic development for all of the Universities and offers positions in all locations. The University of Illinois Foundation is the official fundraising and private gift-receiving agency for the University of Illinois and also offers position in all locations.  Click the links below to search for other University of Illinois positions. University of Illinois Chicago University of Illinois Springfield University of Illinois System Office University of Illinois Foundation Illinois Human Resources University of Illinois Urbana-Champaign Personnel Services Building - MC 562 52 E. Gregory Dr. Champaign, IL  61820 217.333.2137 | jobs@illinois.edu humanresources.illinois.edu"
    },
    "https://illinois.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/1/home/requisition/17565?c=illinois": {
      "title": "Assistant/Associate Professor- Actuarial Science & Risk Management",
      "description": "Assistant/Associate Professor- Actuarial Science & Risk Management | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) Assistant/Associate Professor- Actuarial Science & Risk Management Urbana, IL, United States | 1037103 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 8/11/2026 Back to Search Assistant/Associate Professor Program of Actuarial Science and Risk Management College of Liberal Arts & Sciences University of Illinois at Urbana-Champaign The Program of Actuarial Science and Risk Management at the University of Illinois Urbana-Champaign invites applications for a full time, tenure track assistant professor or tenured associate professor position with an anticipated starting date of August 16, 2027. Illinois has long been recognized as a national leader in actuarial science education. The ASRM program benefits from strong industry partnerships, outstanding student outcomes, continued institutional investment, and an engaged alumni and professional network. This leadership transition comes at a pivotal moment: ASRM has grown into a dynamic and interdisciplinary unit serving over 300 students across undergraduate, master’s, and doctoral programs, and is currently undergoing the approval process to become an independent department within the College of Liberal Arts & Sciences. This open-rank position offers an exciting opportunity to witness the birth of a new department and contribute to its promising future. The successful candidate will contribute to the mission of the College of Liberal Arts & Sciences at the University of Illinois, where curiosity drives impact. As the heart of a leading land-grant research university, LAS brings together diverse disciplines to explore fundamental questions and address complex challenges. We prepare students for a lifetime of inquiry, leadership, and service through innovative research, transformative teaching, and thoughtful mentoring. We strongly encourage applications from those who have demonstrated the knowledge, skills, and experience needed to be effective teachers for our student population with its wide range of backgrounds and experiences, in alignment with the mission of our university. To learn more about the mission, vision, and values of the College of Liberal Arts & Sciences, visit: https://las.illinois.edu . Successful candidates are expected to teach effectively at both the undergraduate and graduate levels, establish and maintain an active and independent research program, and provide service to the department, the university and the profession. Qualifications Required: Applicants must have a Ph.D. in actuarial science, statistics, risk management and insurance, finance, data science or a closely related field before the position start date. Candidates whose PhD may be delayed but will complete all the Ph.D. requirements within the first appointment year may be appointed at the rank of Instructor. After the Ph.D. requirement is met, the appointment will be changed to Assistant Professor. Applicants at the assistant professor level must have a promising research agenda and a commitment to undergraduate and graduate teaching. Applicants at the associate professor level must demonstrate a record of research, teaching and service indicative of a tenured Associate Professor position. Preferred : Willingness to provide service to the unit. We are particularly interested in candidates whose research sits at the intersection of actuarial science and emerging risk and technology. Ideal candidates will exhibit synergy with current faculty expertise or possess the potential to expand our actuarial curriculum. Experience with administrative roles or curriculum development is considered a significant plus. Appointment Information The budgeted salary range for the position is $100,000 to $130,000 at the Assistant Professor level, $130,000 to $160,000 at the Associate Professor level, for a 9-month service basis (paid over 12-months). The pay offered to the selected candidate will be determined based on factors including (but not limited to) the experience and qualifications of the selected candidate, including equivalent years in rank, training, and field or discipline; internal equity; and external market pay for comparable jobs. This position will be expected to work at the University of Illinois Urbana-Champaign campus on a full-time basis per the University’s Workplace Flexibility policy. This position is eligible for sponsorship for work authorization, except for sponsorship of a new H1B petition that would incur the $100,000 fee. To find out more about the resources available at the university and Urbana-Champaign community please visit these sites: Benefits Dual Career Program Explore Champaign-Urbana Work-life balance and family-friendly programs Application Procedures & Deadline Information To apply, create your candidate profile through https://jobs.illinois.edu and submit application materials by November 30, 2026 . Applicants should upload a letter of application addressing how they meet the required and preferred qualifications for this position, as well as a curriculum vitae, up to 3 representative publications, statement of teaching and research interests, and contact information for three professional references. Letters of recommendation may be requested electronically from referees at a later date. Only applications submitted through the University of Illinois Job Board will be considered. We ask that all documents be uploaded in a single .pdf file as an upload in the “Resume/CV” section. Questions regarding the position and application materials may be directed to lascollegehiring@illinois.edu For questions regarding the application portal, please contact 217-333-2137 or jobs@illinois.edu . Founded in 1867 as Illinois’s flagship public university, the University of Illinois Urbana-Champaign empowers a global community of students, scholars, and alumni to change the world through bold, innovative research and transformative education. With a land-grant heritage rooted in progress, Illinois faculty drive paradigm-shifting discoveries, mentor future leaders, and collaborate across 15 colleges and instructional units and more than 20 research institutes. The university’s legacy of excellence includes 24 Nobel Prizes and 29 Pulitzer Prizes awarded to its faculty and alumni, $755 million in sponsored research funding, and 94 academic programs ranked in the top 20 nationally. Illinois offers the resources, recognition, and reach to accelerate your career — along with a highly competitive benefits portfolio. Discover how the Illinois Value Proposition fosters professional longevity, personal fulfillment, and a deep sense of purpose in every role. Faculty Recruitment Champaign-Urbana The University of Illinois\nmust also comply with applicable federal export control laws and regulations\nand, as such, reserves the right to employ restricted party screening\nprocedures for applicants. Artificial Intelligence (AI) tools may be used in some portions of the candidate review process for this position; however, all employment decisions will be made by a person. This position is intended to be eligible for benefits . This includes Health, Dental, Vision, Life Insurance, a Retirement Plan, Paid time Off, and Tuition waivers for employees and dependents. The University of Illinois System is an equal opportunity employer, including but not limited to disability and/or veteran status, and complies with all applicable state and federal employment mandates. Please visit Required Employment Notices and Posters to view our non-discrimination statement and find additional information about required background checks, sexual harassment/misconduct disclosures, and employment eligibility review through E-Verify . Applicants with disabilities are encouraged to apply and may request a reasonable accommodation under the Americans with Disabilities Act (2008) to complete the application and/or interview process. Accommodations may also be requested on the basis of pregnancy, childbirth, and related conditions, or religion. Requests may be submitted through the reasonable accommodation portal , or by contacting the Office for Access & Equity at 217-333-0885, option #1, or accessibility@illinois.edu . Requisition ID : 1037103 Job Category : Faculty Apply at: https://jobs.illinois.edu Apply Now Share Save Job Looking for more University of Illinois Positions? We invite you to search for positions at each of the University of Illinois' locations, the University of Illinois System Office and the University of Illinois Foundation. The University of Illinois System Office supports the primary missions of teaching, research, public service, and economic development for all of the Universities and offers positions in all locations. The University of Illinois Foundation is the official fundraising and private gift-receiving agency for the University of Illinois and also offers position in all locations.  Click the links below to search for other University of Illinois positions. University of Illinois Chicago University of Illinois Springfield University of Illinois System Office University of Illinois Foundation Illinois Human Resources University of Illinois Urbana-Champaign Personnel Services Building - MC 562 52 E. Gregory Dr. Champaign, IL  61820 217.333.2137 | jobs@illinois.edu humanresources.illinois.edu"
    },
    "https://illinois.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/1/home/requisition/17569?c=illinois": {
      "title": "Associate/Full Professor- Classics",
      "description": "Associate/Full Professor- Classics | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) Associate/Full Professor- Classics Urbana, IL, United States | 1037105 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 8/6/2026 Back to Search Associate/Full Professor Department of Classics College of Liberal Arts & Sciences University of Illinois at Urbana-Champaign The Classics Department at the University of Illinois Urbana-Champaign invites applications for a full-time, tenured position at the rank of Associate or Full Professor, with any research specialization in Classical Studies. Preference will be given to advanced Associate Professors and Full Professors. Exceptional candidates may be considered for the Robert D. Novak Chair of Western Civilization and Culture . The person hired will contribute to our highly successful general education curriculum by regularly teaching a large-enrollment class on Greek and Roman mythology as well as other courses in Classical Civilization and, depending on specialization, Greek, Latin, or material culture, at both undergraduate and graduate levels; the teaching load is 2-2. Preference will be given to applicants who have built an international reputation as a scholar, as well as a record of outstanding teaching, particularly in large format lecture classes. The successful candidate will contribute to the mission of the College of Liberal Arts and Sciences. As the heart of a leading land-grant research university, LAS brings together diverse disciplines to explore fundamental questions and address complex challenges. We prepare students for a lifetime of inquiry, leadership, and service through innovative research, transformative teaching, and thoughtful mentoring. We strongly encourage applications from those who have demonstrated the knowledge, skills, and experience needed to be effective teachers for our student population with its wide range of backgrounds and experiences, in alignment with the mission of our university. To learn more about the mission, vision, and values of the College of Liberal Arts & Sciences, visit: https://las.illinois.edu . The College of Liberal Arts and Sciences prioritizes hiring faculty who contribute to the excellence of the university and foster an inclusive learning environment through their research, teaching, and/or service. Applicants to this position must present evidence of accomplishment in these areas. The appointee will be expected to maintain a distinguished publication record, teach effectively at both undergraduate and graduate levels, perform administrative duties associated with our B.A, M.A., and Ph.D. programs, and participate in our department's activities in the areas of student mentorship, curricular innovation, and interdisciplinary collaboration. Applicants must have a Ph.D. and research and teaching record in Classics or a closely related field. In general, we will give higher priority to the overall originality and impact of applicants' work rather than to the area of specialization. Appointment Information The anticipated start date is August 16, 2027, but is flexible based on the successful applicant's needs. The budgeted salary range for the position is $100,000 to $120,000 at the Associate Professor level, and $120,000 to $165,000 at the Full Professor level, on a 9-month service basis paid over 12 months . The pay offered to the selected candidate will be determined based on factors including (but not limited to) their experience and qualifications, including years in rank; internal equity; and external market pay for comparable jobs. The person hired will be expected to work at the University of Illinois Urbana-Champaign campus on a full-time basis per the University’s Workplace Flexibility policy. This position is eligible for sponsorship for work authorization, except for sponsorship of a new H1B petition that would incur the $100,000 fee. Application Procedures & Deadline Information To apply, create your candidate profile through https://jobs.illinois.edu . Only applications submitted through this portal will be considered. To ensure full consideration, applicants should upload the following materials by 11:59 pm (CST) on October 1, 2026 : a letter of application a curriculum vitae a statement of research interests a statement of teaching philosophy, as well as evidence of accomplishment in teaching, particularly in a large lecture format, such as peer evaluations, student feedback, and/or teaching materials created contact information for three professional references We ask that all documents be uploaded in a single PDF file in the “Resume/CV” section. Short-listed applicants will be contacted by email in order to schedule interviews on Zoom and to arrange for three letters of reference to be sent to the search committee. We anticipate that finalists' visits to campus will take place in November and early December. The Classics Department is a thriving community of teacher-scholars, and our university has extensive library holdings in Classics and related fields, as well as two museums with excellent collections of ancient Mediterranean artifacts. Questions are welcome and should be addressed to Prof. Craig Williams, Chair of the Search Committee (cawllms@illinois.edu). Additional information about our department can be found at classics.illinois.edu . For further information regarding application procedures, you may contact lascollegehiring@illinois.edu . For questions regarding the application portal, please contact 217-333-2137 or jobs@illinois.edu. To find out more about the resources available at the university and Urbana-Champaign community please visit these sites: Benefits Dual Career Program Explore Champaign-Urbana Work-life balance and family-friendly programs The University of Illinois must comply with applicable federal export control laws and regulations and, as such, reserves the right to employ restricted party screening procedures for applicants. Artificial Intelligence (AI) tools may be used in some portions of the candidate review process for this position; however, all employment decisions will be made by a person. This position is intended to be eligible for benefits . This includes health, dental, vision, life insurance, a retirement plan, paid time off, and tuition waivers for employees and dependents. This position is intended to be eligible for benefits . This includes Health, Dental, Vision, Life Insurance, a Retirement Plan, Paid time Off, and Tuition waivers for employees and dependents. The University of Illinois System is an equal opportunity employer, including but not limited to disability and/or veteran status, and complies with all applicable state and federal employment mandates. Please visit Required Employment Notices and Posters to view our non-discrimination statement and find additional information about required background checks, sexual harassment/misconduct disclosures, and employment eligibility review through E-Verify . Applicants with disabilities are encouraged to apply and may request a reasonable accommodation under the Americans with Disabilities Act (2008) to complete the application and/or interview process. Accommodations may also be requested on the basis of pregnancy, childbirth, and related conditions, or religion. Requests may be submitted through the reasonable accommodation portal , or by contacting the Office for Access & Equity at 217-333-0885, option #1, or accessibility@illinois.edu . Requisition ID : 1037105 Job Category : Faculty Apply at: https://jobs.illinois.edu Apply Now Share Save Job Looking for more University of Illinois Positions? We invite you to search for positions at each of the University of Illinois' locations, the University of Illinois System Office and the University of Illinois Foundation. The University of Illinois System Office supports the primary missions of teaching, research, public service, and economic development for all of the Universities and offers positions in all locations. The University of Illinois Foundation is the official fundraising and private gift-receiving agency for the University of Illinois and also offers position in all locations.  Click the links below to search for other University of Illinois positions. University of Illinois Chicago University of Illinois Springfield University of Illinois System Office University of Illinois Foundation Illinois Human Resources University of Illinois Urbana-Champaign Personnel Services Building - MC 562 52 E. Gregory Dr. Champaign, IL  61820 217.333.2137 | jobs@illinois.edu humanresources.illinois.edu"
