    "https://illinois.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/1/home/requisition/18312?c=illinois": {
      "title": "Assistant/Associate Professor, Contemporary Art History (1980-present, open geographic focus)",
      "description": "Assistant/Associate Professor, Contemporary Art History (1980-present, open geographic focus) | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) Assistant/Associate Professor, Contemporary Art History (1980-present, open geographic focus) Urbana, IL, United States | 1038959 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 10/23/2026 Back to Search Assistant or Associate Professor, Contemporary Art History (1980-present, open geographic focus) School of Art & Design College of Fine & Applied Arts University of Illinois Urbana-Champaign The Art History Program in the School of Art & Design at the University of Illinois at Urbana-Champaign ( https://art.illinois.edu ) invites applications for a full-time, tenure-track position at the rank of Assistant or Associate Professor of Art History, with specialization in contemporary art (1980-present, open geographic focus). In addition to maintaining an active research program, the successful candidate will teach undergraduate and graduate courses on contemporary art with a global perspective, introductory courses in art history and visual culture, and upper-level seminars in their areas of expertise. We will prioritize candidates whose work expands the program’s methodological and geographic scope, and we especially encourage applications from those who engage with topics such as gender and sexuality, queer and trans theory, race, postcoloniality, decoloniality, diaspora, migration, Indigeneity, and ecology. Candidates whose research includes a curatorial practice are welcome. Responsibilities include a 2/2 teaching load (two courses per semester), mentorship of students at all levels, supervision of Ph.D. dissertations and M.A. theses, and contribution to the vitality and administration of the program, school, and university. The Art History Program currently consists of seven full-time tenured/tenure-track faculty members, plus affiliated faculty. Degrees offered include the B.A., B.F.A, M.A., and Ph.D. The Program works closely with studio-art, design, and art-education programs in the School of Art & Design , as well as collaborating with colleagues in the Krannert Art Museum and the Spurlock Museum. Faculty are often affiliated with other units and interdisciplinary centers on campus, such as the Center for African Studies; Center for East Asian and Pacific Studies; Center for Latin American and Caribbean Studies; Center for South Asian and Middle Eastern Studies; Center for the Study of Global Gender Equity; European Union Center; Holocaust, Genocide, and Memory Studies; Humanities Research Institute; Illinois Global Institute; Lemann Center for Brazilian Studies; Russian, Eastern European, and Eurasian Center; and the Unit for Criticism and Interpretive Theory. About the College of Fine and Applied Arts The College of Fine and Applied Arts (FAA) is singular in the nation for its diversity, innovation and breadth. Its mission is dedicated to the advancement, practice, and understanding of the arts, and its central focus is the synergy between research and the preparation of students for professional careers in the creation and interpretation of the environmental, visual, and performing arts. Deeply related to that focus is the commitment to elevate and sustain the study of the arts as both a necessary mode of understanding and a vibrant expression of human experience within the local, national, and international communities. The college comprises the Schools of Music , Architecture , and Art and Design ; Departments of Dance , Landscape Architecture , Theatre , and Urban and Regional Planning ; the Sustainable Design program; Krannert Center for the Performing Arts ; Krannert Art Museum ; and Japan House . This unique constellation of academic, research, and cultural institutions creates exceptional opportunities for interdisciplinary collaboration across the arts, design, technology, culture, and the built environment. FAA employs more than 660 faculty and staff members, including more than 150 tenure-system faculty, and serves more than 1,850 undergraduate students and 635 graduate students enrolled across more than 30 majors and 10 minors. The College provides a vibrant environment for innovative teaching, scholarly inquiry, creative practice, and public engagement, making it an ideal setting for advancing the future of industrial design education, research, and professional practice. Qualifications Required: A Ph.D. in Art History or a related field (for example, Gender and Sexuality Studies, Latin American Studies, Media Studies, etc.) by the start of the appointment is required. The successful candidate will have an active and innovative research program and demonstrated capacity to teach courses on contemporary art for art-history, studio-art, and design students, as well as to mentor M.A. and Ph.D. students in art history. Candidates applying at the Associate level should have a strong record of publication and an ongoing research program. Preferred: Research and teaching expertise that expands the program’s methodological and geographic scope is preferred. We strongly encourage applications from individuals with demonstrable commitments to equity and social justice through teaching, research, and/or community engagement, and a reflective approach to transforming the discipline with respect to inclusion and anti-racism. We encourage applications from candidates of all backgrounds who bring experience working with under-represented and underserved communities and traditions. Institutional Context The University of Illinois is an internationally recognized research and educational institution located in Urbana-Champaign, a vibrant university community within driving distance of Chicago, Indianapolis, and St. Louis. With the nation’s third largest research library, the University supports faculty as active researchers in the humanities, arts, sciences, and engineering through opportunities for funding and vital cross-disciplinary exchange in the campus’ many institutes, centers, and initiatives. These include the Siebel Center for Design, Campus Research Board, the Illinois Program for Research in the Humanities, the Center for Advanced Study, the Beckman Institute for Advanced Science and Technology, and numerous other specialized centers. Additional collaborative opportunities include Krannert Art Museum and the Krannert Center for the Performing Arts, each a respected international hub for innovative scholarship and public engagement. For more information, please visit https://illinois.edu/ for the University, https://faa.illinois.edu/ for the College, and https://art.illinois.edu for the School of Art & Design. Salary and Appointment Information This is a nine-month faculty appointment (paid over 12 months). The anticipated start date is August 16, 2027. The salary range for the Assistant Professor position is\n$76,000-$85,000 and the salary range for the Associate Professor is\n$92,000-$105,000. We strive to provide a competitive salary, considering\nfactors such as available market data, internal equity, candidate’s experience\nand qualifications, and budget constraints. Sponsorship options. This position is eligible for sponsorship for work authorization, except for sponsorship of a new H1B petition that would incur the $100,000 fee. Application Procedures and Deadline Information Applications must be received by 6:00 pm (CST) on December 1 . Apply for this position using the “Apply Now” button in the job posting at https://jobs.illinois.edu and upload the following items: A letter of application Curriculum vitae Scholarly writing sample List of three references – online application will require names and contact information for three references. Applications not submitted through https://jobs.illinois.edu will not be considered. For further information about this specific position, please contact FAA HR at FAA-HR@illinois.edu . For questions regarding the application process, please contact 217-333-2137. Founded in 1867 as Illinois’s flagship public university, the University of Illinois Urbana-Champaign empowers a global community of students, scholars, and alumni to change the world through bold, innovative research and transformative education. With a land-grant heritage rooted in progress, Illinois faculty drive paradigm-shifting discoveries, mentor future leaders, and collaborate across 15 colleges and instructional units and more than 20 research institutes. The university’s legacy of excellence includes 24 Nobel Prizes and 29 Pulitzer Prizes awarded to its faculty and alumni, $755 million in sponsored research funding, and 94 academic programs ranked in the top 20 nationally. Illinois offers the resources, recognition, and reach to accelerate your career — along with a highly competitive benefits portfolio. Discover how the Illinois Value Proposition fosters professional longevity, personal fulfillment, and a deep sense of purpose in every role. Faculty Recruitment Champaign-Urbana Artificial Intelligence (AI) tools may be used in some portions of the candidate review process for this position; however, all employment decisions will be made by a person. This position is intended to be eligible for benefits . This includes Health, Dental, Vision, Life Insurance, a Retirement Plan, Paid time Off, and Tuition waivers for employees and dependents. The University of Illinois System is an equal opportunity employer, including but not limited to disability and/or veteran status, and complies with all applicable state and federal employment mandates. Please visit Required Employment Notices and Posters to view our non-discrimination statement and find additional information about required background checks, sexual harassment/misconduct disclosures, and employment eligibility review through E-Verify . Applicants with disabilities are encouraged to apply and may request a reasonable accommodation under the Americans with Disabilities Act (2008) to complete the application and/or interview process. Accommodations may also be requested on the basis of pregnancy, childbirth, and related conditions, or religion. Requests may be submitted through the reasonable accommodation portal , or by contacting the Office for Access & Equity at 217-333-0885, option #1, or accessibility@illinois.edu . Requisition ID : 1038959 Job Category : Faculty Apply at: https://jobs.illinois.edu Apply Now Share Save Job Looking for more University of Illinois Positions? We invite you to search for positions at each of the University of Illinois' locations, the University of Illinois System Office and the University of Illinois Foundation. The University of Illinois System Office supports the primary missions of teaching, research, public service, and economic development for all of the Universities and offers positions in all locations. The University of Illinois Foundation is the official fundraising and private gift-receiving agency for the University of Illinois and also offers position in all locations.  Click the links below to search for other University of Illinois positions. University of Illinois Chicago University of Illinois Springfield University of Illinois System Office University of Illinois Foundation Illinois Human Resources University of Illinois Urbana-Champaign Personnel Services Building - MC 562 52 E. Gregory Dr. Champaign, IL  61820 217.333.2137 | jobs@illinois.edu humanresources.illinois.edu"
    },
    "https://illinois.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/1/home/requisition/18007?c=illinois": {
      "title": "The Grainger College of Engineering: Research Assistant Professor - Department of Bioengineering",
      "description": "The Grainger College of Engineering: Research Assistant Professor - Department of Bioengineering | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) The Grainger College of Engineering: Research Assistant Professor - Department of Bioengineering Urbana, IL, United States | 1038368 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 10/22/2026 Back to Search Research Assistant Professor in Cancer Engineering Department of Bioengineering The Grainger College of Engineering University of Illinois Urbana-Champaign The Department of Bioengineering in the Grainger College of Engineering at the University of Illinois Urbana-Champaign invites applications for a full-time Research Assistant Professor in cancer engineering. The successful candidate will join a research group that is focused on using engineering methods to make cancer models and measuring them using novel forms of imaging. Projects in the group include those supported by The Advanced Research Projects Agency for Health (ARPA-H), National Science Foundation (NSF), and National Institutes of Health (NIH). The successful candidate will carry out responsibilities related to research and public service. As part of the larger research group, they will carry out research and educational administration to support the entire team. They will be expected to also establish and maintain an active and independent research program. Research track faculty in the Department of Bioengineering are expected to provide professional leadership within the department, other campus units, and the professional community. There is a strong track record of support for this research group from NSF, NIH and ARPA-H at Illinois, and we are seeking applications from individuals who are eager to engage with this collaborative community. Significant funding has resulted in a demand for dedicated scientific leadership, and the individual in this role will provide leadership, project management, supervision of personnel, and sustained growth of the research enterprise which provide outstanding opportunities related to this research. This role is critical to the successful execution and long-term sustainability of funded research activities. This position joins a department that is experiencing a period of programmatic growth, including significant increases in course offerings and student numbers in both graduate and undergraduate programs. With the completion of new facilities and strong partnerships with Carle Illinois College of Medicine and the Cancer Center at Illinois , there are numerous opportunities to impact valuable research. A doctoral degree in Bioengineering, Chemistry, Materials Science and Engineering or a related field is required at the start date. The budgeted salary range for the position is $80,000 to $95,000, for a 9-month service basis paid over 12 months. Salary is competitive and commensurate with qualifications and experience, while also considering internal equity. Full consideration will be given to applications received by November 5, 2026. Applications may be reviewed as they are received. Those submitted after the stated deadline may still be considered until the position is filled. Applicants may be interviewed before the closing date; however, no hiring decision will be made until after that date. A start date is expected as soon as possible after the close date; however, this is negotiable. This position is eligible for sponsorship for work authorization. Application Procedures & Deadline Information To apply for this position, please create a candidate profile at https://jobs.illinois.edu. The application package should include the following materials uploaded as a single PDF file in the “Resume/CV” section: 1) cover letter, 2) curriculum vitae, 3) research statement, 4) service statement, and 5) names and contact information for three professional references (no letters required at this time). The research and service statements offer a chance to share your motivation, approach, experience, leadership, impact, and vision in each area, including how you would support the university’s land-grant mission ( https://boldly.illinois.edu/ ), through campus, community, or professional engagement. For further information  regarding application procedures, please address questions to Kathy Atwood at kbuss@illinois.edu . Founded in 1867 as Illinois’s flagship public university, the University of Illinois Urbana-Champaign empowers a global community of students, scholars, and alumni to change the world through bold, innovative research and transformative education. With a land-grant heritage rooted in progress, Illinois faculty drive paradigm-shifting discoveries, mentor future leaders, and collaborate across 15 colleges and instructional units and more than 20 research institutes. The university’s legacy of excellence includes 24 Nobel Prizes and 29 Pulitzer Prizes awarded to its faculty and alumni, $755 million in sponsored research funding, and 94 academic programs ranked in the top 20 nationally. Illinois offers the resources, recognition, and reach to accelerate your career — along with a highly competitive benefits portfolio. Discover how the Illinois Value Proposition fosters professional longevity, personal fulfillment, and a deep sense of purpose in every role. Faculty Recruitment Champaign-Urbana Artificial Intelligence (AI) tools may be used in some portions of the candidate review process for this position; however, all employment decisions will be made by a person. This position is intended to be eligible for benefits . This includes Health, Dental, Vision, Life Insurance, a Retirement Plan, Paid time Off, and Tuition waivers for employees and dependents. The University of Illinois System is an equal opportunity employer, including but not limited to disability and/or veteran status, and complies with all applicable state and federal employment mandates. Please visit Required Employment Notices and Posters to view our non-discrimination statement and find additional information about required background checks, sexual harassment/misconduct disclosures, and employment eligibility review through E-Verify . Applicants with disabilities are encouraged to apply and may request a reasonable accommodation under the Americans with Disabilities Act (2008) to complete the application and/or interview process. Accommodations may also be requested on the basis of pregnancy, childbirth, and related conditions, or religion. Requests may be submitted through the reasonable accommodation portal , or by contacting the Office for Access & Equity at 217-333-0885, option #1, or accessibility@illinois.edu . Requisition ID : 1038368 Job Category : Faculty Apply at: https://jobs.illinois.edu Apply Now Share Save Job Looking for more University of Illinois Positions? We invite you to search for positions at each of the University of Illinois' locations, the University of Illinois System Office and the University of Illinois Foundation. The University of Illinois System Office supports the primary missions of teaching, research, public service, and economic development for all of the Universities and offers positions in all locations. The University of Illinois Foundation is the official fundraising and private gift-receiving agency for the University of Illinois and also offers position in all locations.  Click the links below to search for other University of Illinois positions. University of Illinois Chicago University of Illinois Springfield University of Illinois System Office University of Illinois Foundation Illinois Human Resources University of Illinois Urbana-Champaign Personnel Services Building - MC 562 52 E. Gregory Dr. Champaign, IL  61820 217.333.2137 | jobs@illinois.edu humanresources.illinois.edu"
    },
    "https://illinois.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/1/home/requisition/18154?c=illinois": {
      "title": "Open-Rank Tenure-Track Faculty Position in Information Systems, Operations Management, Supply Chain",
      "description": "Open-Rank Tenure-Track Faculty Position in Information Systems, Operations Management, Supply Chain | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) Open-Rank Tenure-Track Faculty Position in Information Systems, Operations Management, Supply Chain Urbana, IL, United States | 1038657 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 10/21/2026 Back to Search Open-Rank Tenure-Track Faculty Position in Information Systems, Operations Management, Supply Chain Management, & Analytics (IOSA) Area UNIVERSITY OF ILLINOIS URBANA-CHAMPAIGN, Gies College of Business, Department of Business Administration Applications are invited from qualified individuals for a 100% full-time open rank, tenure-track professor position in Information Systems, Operations Management, Supply Chain Management, & Analytics (IOSA) area within the Department of Business Administration. We are interested in candidates who will bring excellence to campus via outstanding research, teaching, and service. We seek candidates with a demonstrated commitment to research excellence. Research methods can include but are not restricted to traditional and cutting-edge methods such as empirical methods, behavioral or field experiments, machine learning, operations research, game theory, and/or related methods with particular emphasis on applications in information systems, operations, and supply chain management. Priority will be given to candidates whose research leverages AI/ML methodologies, advanced analytics, and data-driven decision making to solve contemporary business challenges. We especially welcome candidates who can bridge traditional business disciplines with emerging AI and analytics applications. An ability and openness to teach courses at graduate and undergraduate levels with different delivery formats is desirable. Experience with online teaching is valued but not required. Qualified candidates will have completed a Ph.D. in Business Administration, Information Systems, Business Analytics, Operations Management, Supply Chain Management, or a closely related field. The Gies College of Business at Illinois is a world leader in research, teaching, and public engagement. We serve the state, the nation, and the world by creating knowledge, preparing students for lives of impact, and addressing critical societal needs through the transfer and application of knowledge. In 2020, the Gies iMBA program was named one of the top ten \"Biggest B-School Innovations of The Decade” by Poets and Quants. The college has also become a leader in experiential learning. Gies provides the environment and resources that foster meaningful actions, empower students to make their mark, and put their purpose into practice – to make the world a better place. Gies Business is committed to being a model for fostering an inclusive and equitable community, and supporting initiatives that promote access, belonging, and respectful engagement. We strive to prepare future business leaders to work effectively in diverse environments and to engage thoughtfully with our community and corporate partners. We are interested in candidates who will bring excellence via outstanding research, teaching, and service. The Department of Business Administration is a diverse and growing unit, which includes graduate and undergraduate programs across seven academic areas (i.e., Organizational Behavior, Strategic Management, International Business, Marketing, Operations Management, Information Systems, and Supply Chain). Additional information about the Department may be found here . SPECIFIC DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES Maintain an active and productive program of research. Teach at the graduate and undergraduate levels. Perform service for the department. Provide leadership in the department and the university. MINIMUM QUALIFICATIONS Candidates at advanced ranks must possess a Ph.D. degree; candidates for assistant professor should expect to have completed their doctoral degree by June 1, 2027. Strong research portfolio. Demonstrated teaching effectiveness. Leadership potential commensurate with position sought. SALARY AND APPOINTMENT INFORMATION This is a 9-month, 100%-time academic tenure-track position with the opportunity for summer appointment. The expected start date is August 16, 2027 . The budgeted salary range for this position is $200,000-$220,000 at the Assistant Professor level or $210,000-$240,000 at the Associate Professor level, and $230,000-$280,000 at the Professor level The pay offered to the selected candidate will be determined based on factors including (but not limited to) the experience and qualifications of the selected candidate including equivalent years in rank, training, and field or discipline; internal equity; and external market pay for comparable jobs. This position is eligible for visa sponsorship except for sponsorship of a new H1B petition that would incur the $100,000 fee. APPLICATION PROCEDURES & DEADLINE INFORMATION For full consideration, please submit a cover letter, curriculum vitae, contact information of three professional references, and evidence of past teaching success. Applications must be received by 6:00 pm (Central Time) on November 21, 2026 . Applications and supplemental materials must be submitted online at https://jobs.illinois.edu . Only applications submitted through the University of Illinois Job Board will be considered. Doctoral candidates must also email business-bahr@business.illinois.edu to have their references requested through the application system. Additionally, if you would like the committee to be aware of any conference presentations, please include this information in the letter of intent. Interviews may occur prior to the initial closing date; however, the review of applications will continue until suitable candidates are identified. For further information about this specific position, please contact Stephanie Overmier at business-bahr@business.illinois.edu . For questions regarding the application process, please contact 217-333-2137. Founded in 1867 as Illinois’s flagship public university, the University of Illinois Urbana-Champaign empowers a global community of students, scholars, and alumni to change the world through bold, innovative research and transformative education. With a land-grant heritage rooted in progress, Illinois faculty drive paradigm-shifting discoveries, mentor future leaders, and collaborate across 15 colleges and instructional units and more than 20 research institutes. The university’s legacy of excellence includes 24 Nobel Prizes and 29 Pulitzer Prizes awarded to its faculty and alumni, $755 million in sponsored research funding, and 94 academic programs ranked in the top 20 nationally. Illinois offers the resources, recognition, and reach to accelerate your career — along with a highly competitive benefits portfolio. Discover how the Illinois Value Proposition fosters professional longevity, personal fulfillment, and a deep sense of purpose in every role. Faculty Recruitment Champaign-Urbana Artificial Intelligence (AI) tools may be used in some portions of the candidate review process for this position; however, all employment decisions will be made by a person. This position is intended to be eligible for benefits . This includes Health, Dental, Vision, Life Insurance, a Retirement Plan, Paid time Off, and Tuition waivers for employees and dependents. The University of Illinois System is an equal opportunity employer, including but not limited to disability and/or veteran status, and complies with all applicable state and federal employment mandates. Please visit Required Employment Notices and Posters to view our non-discrimination statement and find additional information about required background checks, sexual harassment/misconduct disclosures, and employment eligibility review through E-Verify . Applicants with disabilities are encouraged to apply and may request a reasonable accommodation under the Americans with Disabilities Act (2008) to complete the application and/or interview process. Accommodations may also be requested on the basis of pregnancy, childbirth, and related conditions, or religion. Requests may be submitted through the reasonable accommodation portal , or by contacting the Office for Access & Equity at 217-333-0885, option #1, or accessibility@illinois.edu . Requisition ID : 1038657 Job Category : Faculty Apply at: https://jobs.illinois.edu Apply Now Share Save Job Looking for more University of Illinois Positions? We invite you to search for positions at each of the University of Illinois' locations, the University of Illinois System Office and the University of Illinois Foundation. The University of Illinois System Office supports the primary missions of teaching, research, public service, and economic development for all of the Universities and offers positions in all locations. The University of Illinois Foundation is the official fundraising and private gift-receiving agency for the University of Illinois and also offers position in all locations.  Click the links below to search for other University of Illinois positions. University of Illinois Chicago University of Illinois Springfield University of Illinois System Office University of Illinois Foundation Illinois Human Resources University of Illinois Urbana-Champaign Personnel Services Building - MC 562 52 E. Gregory Dr. Champaign, IL  61820 217.333.2137 | jobs@illinois.edu humanresources.illinois.edu"
    },
    "https://illinois.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/1/home/requisition/18214?c=illinois": {
      "title": "Clinical Associate/Full Professor and Director of Clinical Education & Operations - Department of Sp",
      "description": "Clinical Associate/Full Professor and Director of Clinical Education & Operations - Department of Sp | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) Clinical Associate/Full Professor and Director of Clinical Education & Operations - Department of Sp Urbana, IL, United States | 1038792 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 10/19/2026 Back to Search Clinical\nAssociate/Full Professor and Director of Clinical Education and Operations Department of Speech and Hearing Science College of Applied Health Sciences University of Illinois at Champaign-Urbana The University of Illinois\nDepartment of Speech and Hearing Science (SHS) (http://shs.illinois.edu) is seeking to recruit an\noutstanding Director of Clinical Education and Operations for a full-time,\n12-month non-tenure-track position at the rank of Clinical Associate/Clinical\nFull Professor. The Department of Speech and Hearing Science is widely recognized as\namong the top departments in the nation, conducts cutting-edge research across\nthe entire spectrum of human communication, has excellent academic programs at\nthe undergraduate, master’s, and doctorate levels, and offers accredited\ngraduate clinical programs in speech-language pathology and audiology. We seek a visionary and\ncollaborative clinical leader to shape the future of our Speech-Language &\nAudiology Clinic by advancing excellence in clinical care and education and\nsupporting strategic, sustainable growth. Available Start Date This position will be available beginning July 1, 2027. Description The Director of Clinical\nEducation and Operations will oversee and advance clinical education for\nthe MA in Speech-Language Pathology Program, as well as day-to-day\noperations of the Speech-Language and Audiology Clinic. The Director will also\nfacilitate work with clinical and academic faculty to promote translational\nresearch in the Departmental clinic, and to direct and promote outreach\nactivities on behalf of the Department and Clinic. The Director will advance\nprogrammatic clinical needs primarily at the graduate level. Responsibilities The Director\nof Clinical Education and Operations will have responsibilities that include: overseeing and\ncoordinating graduate student clinical education, including clinical program\ndevelopment and accreditation oversight; directing and overseeing operations of the Speech-Language\n& Audiology Clinic, including budget management, service reimbursement,\nhiring and supervision of clinical staff; and supporting translational research and scholarly efforts across the Department.\nSpecific responsibilities of this role include but are not limited to: Develop, plan, coordinate, facilitate, and evaluate clinical education activities and services in coordination with clinical and academic faculty. Monitor student clinical progress and assess performance. Provide guidance and support as required to problem-solve and address pertinent issues with students, clinical educators, and department administrators. Participate in local, statewide, and national service and scholarship activities to advance the educational and service missions of the Department. Lead and evaluate community outreach activities that advance the educational, clinical service, and community engagement mission of the Department and Clinic. Maintain knowledge of current research trends in healthcare and education and their implications on clinical education. Teach courses in the M.A. in Speech-Language Pathology program and provide supervised clinical services in the Speech-Language & Audiology Clinic consistent with area(s) of expertise. Manage academic and administrative responsibilities to ensure compliance with CAA, federal/state, institutional policy, and practice setting requirements. Coordinate clinic budget management (with Department Head and College Business Office) to understand the impact of insurance and service delivery changes. Provide oversight of Clinic operations and regulatory compliance, including electronic health record and patient records management; billing, collections, insurance reimbursement, and related financial processes; and security, occupational health and safety, and other applicable requirements. Provide administrative and operational leadership for the Clinic, including hiring, training, and supervising administrative staff; coordinating clinical faculty and staff meetings and annual staff performance reviews; and collaborating with leadership to develop business strategies and patient services. Qualifications Applicants\nmust hold a master’s degree in\nSpeech-Language Pathology, with preference for a doctoral degree in\nCommunication Sciences and Disorders or a related field. The applicant must\nhold ASHA certification in the area of Speech-Language Pathology (CCC-SLP) and\nbe licensed or eligible for IL state licensure in Speech-Language Pathology.\nIdeal candidates have at least seven years of experience working in clinical\neducation of graduate students, as well as experience directing clinical\neducation and clinical services in a fee-for-service University Clinic. Appointment Information This is a 100% full-time Academic position, appointed on a 12-month basis. The expected start date is July 1, 2027. The salary range for this position is $100,000 – $125,000. Final salary offered will be determined by a thorough assessment of available market data, internal salary equity, candidate experience and qualifications, collective bargaining agreements, and budget constraints. This position is not eligible for any type of sponsorship for work authorization. Application Procedures & Deadline Information Applications must be received by 6:00 pm (Central Time) on December 2, 2026. Apply for this position using the Apply Now button at the top or bottom of this posting. Applications not submitted through https://jobs.illinois.edu will not be considered. For\nfull consideration, an application must be received by December 2, 2026. The following materials\nare required: (1) a cover letter that includes a summary of qualifications for\nthe position; (2) a statement of clinical and teaching philosophy and\nexperience; (3) a curriculum vitae; and (4) names and contact information for\nthree references. Candidates will be notified before letters of\nrecommendation are requested. Applications may\nbe reviewed upon receipt, but decisions will not be made until after the close\ndate.  Review of applications\nwill continue until the position is filled. For further information about this specific position, applicants may contact: Jaime Bauer Malandraki, MS, MS, CCC-SLP, BCS-S Clinical Professor\n| Chair, Search Committee Phone:\n217-300-3321; Email: jaimebm@illinois.edu For questions regarding the application process, please contact 217-333-2137. Academic Environment Speech and Hearing Science is a state and\nnational leader in clinical education and research and a highly collegial and\ncollaborative department, situated in the College of Applied Health Sciences on\nthe main campus of the University of Illinois in Urbana-Champaign and includes\n(a) the recently renovated Speech and Hearing Science building that houses\nacademic, research, and collaborative spaces; (b) the Audiology &\nSpeech-Language Pathology Clinic; and (c) the Collaboration Lab that houses\nclinical faculty offices, a classroom, multiple study spaces for clinical\ngraduate students, and private spaces for tele-practice. The department offers\nan undergraduate degree and three graduate degrees—M.A., Au.D., and Ph.D. Its\nmission is to engage in research, education, and outreach activities that\nenhance communication across the lifespan, integrating research and clinical\napplications from the biological, behavioral, and social sciences. Our faculty\nare committed to advancing diversity in professional practice and the\nprofessoriate. SHS upholds excellence and distinction across all degree\nprograms, fosters faculty mentorship and professional growth, and encourages\nengagement at the state, national, and international levels. Visit http://www.shs.illinois.edu for additional information about the\ndepartment and its programs. Departmental activities contribute to the\nmission of the College, specifically, the advancement of research, instruction,\nand public engagement that promotes the development of healthy, livable\ncommunities, facilitates optimal living with a disability, and promotes health\nand wellness across the lifespan and throughout a diverse society. The College\nhouses two interdisciplinary research centers, the Center on\nHealth, Aging, and Disability and the Chez Veterans Center, and\nhouses the Division of Disability Resources and Educational Services. The University of Illinois offers generous\nemployee benefits (https://www.hr.uillinois.edu/benefits/) including health insurance and retirement programs. In addition, we also\noffer our employees tuition waivers and other development opportunities\nfor personal and professional growth. The University assists faculty spouses\nand partners seeking employment through our Dual Career Program (https://humanresources.illinois.edu/dual-career-program/). To learn more about all Champaign-Urbana has\nto offer, please visit https://yourewelcomecu.com. We value our employees and seek to foster\nan inclusive workplace. Founded in 1867 as Illinois’s flagship public university, the University of Illinois Urbana-Champaign empowers a global community of students, scholars, and alumni to change the world through bold, innovative research and transformative education. With a land-grant heritage rooted in progress, Illinois faculty drive paradigm-shifting discoveries, mentor future leaders, and collaborate across 15 colleges and instructional units and more than 20 research institutes. The university’s legacy of excellence includes 24 Nobel Prizes and 29 Pulitzer Prizes awarded to its faculty and alumni, $755 million in sponsored research funding, and 94 academic programs ranked in the top 20 nationally. Illinois offers the resources, recognition, and reach to accelerate your career — along with a highly competitive benefits portfolio. Discover how the Illinois Value Proposition fosters professional longevity, personal fulfillment, and a deep sense of purpose in every role. Faculty Recruitment Champaign-Urbana Artificial Intelligence (AI) tools may be used in some portions of the candidate review process for this position; however, all employment decisions will be made by a person. This position is intended to be eligible for benefits . This includes Health, Dental, Vision, Life Insurance, a Retirement Plan, Paid time Off, and Tuition waivers for employees and dependents. The University of Illinois System is an equal opportunity employer, including but not limited to disability and/or veteran status, and complies with all applicable state and federal employment mandates. Please visit Required Employment Notices and Posters to view our non-discrimination statement and find additional information about required background checks, sexual harassment/misconduct disclosures, and employment eligibility review through E-Verify . Applicants with disabilities are encouraged to apply and may request a reasonable accommodation under the Americans with Disabilities Act (2008) to complete the application and/or interview process. Accommodations may also be requested on the basis of pregnancy, childbirth, and related conditions, or religion. Requests may be submitted through the reasonable accommodation portal , or by contacting the Office for Access & Equity at 217-333-0885, option #1, or accessibility@illinois.edu . Requisition ID : 1038792 Job Category : Faculty Apply at: https://jobs.illinois.edu Apply Now Share Save Job Looking for more University of Illinois Positions? We invite you to search for positions at each of the University of Illinois' locations, the University of Illinois System Office and the University of Illinois Foundation. The University of Illinois System Office supports the primary missions of teaching, research, public service, and economic development for all of the Universities and offers positions in all locations. The University of Illinois Foundation is the official fundraising and private gift-receiving agency for the University of Illinois and also offers position in all locations.  Click the links below to search for other University of Illinois positions. University of Illinois Chicago University of Illinois Springfield University of Illinois System Office University of Illinois Foundation Illinois Human Resources University of Illinois Urbana-Champaign Personnel Services Building - MC 562 52 E. Gregory Dr. Champaign, IL  61820 217.333.2137 | jobs@illinois.edu humanresources.illinois.edu"
    },
    "https://illinois.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/1/home/requisition/17712?c=illinois": {
      "title": "Associate/Full Tenure Track Faculty in Marketing",
      "description": "Associate/Full Tenure Track Faculty in Marketing | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) Associate/Full Tenure Track Faculty in Marketing Urbana, IL, United States | 1037877 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 10/27/2026 Back to Search Associate/Full\nTenure Track Faculty in Marketing UNIVERSITY OF\nILLINOIS URBANA-CHAMPAIGN Gies College\nof Business, Department of Business Administration Gies College of Business at the University of Illinois invites applications from qualified individuals for a 100% full-time tenured Associate or Full Professor position in Marketing within the Department of Business Administration. The Gies College of Business serves the state, the nation, and the world by creating knowledge, preparing students for lives of impact, and addressing critical societal needs through the transfer and application of knowledge. We are interested in candidates who will bring excellence to campus via outstanding research, teaching, and service. The successful candidate will support the academic excellence of this well-respected department. This includes a record of visible and rigorous scholarly achievement appropriate for the candidate’s rank; contributing to the innovation in programs and curricula for which the department is known; delivering an exceptional experience to highly motivated students; and advancing the College’s strategic priorities. The University of Illinois offers an outstanding tradition of scholarship and a supportive environment for faculty development and excellence. The Gies College of Business at Illinois is a world leader in research, teaching, and public engagement. We offer exceptional support for data collection, data acquisition, and programming through the Gies Behavioral Research Lab, Data Science Research Services, and numerous other well-resourced units. In 2020, the Gies iMBA program was named one of the top ten \"Biggest B-School Innovations of The Decade” by Poets and Quants. The college has also become a leader in experiential learning. Gies provides the environment and resources that foster meaningful actions, empower students to make their mark, and put their purpose into practice – to make the world a better place. Gies Business is committed to being a model for fostering an inclusive and equitable community, and supporting initiatives that promote access, belonging, and respectful engagement. We strive to prepare future business leaders to work effectively in diverse environments and to engage thoughtfully with our community and corporate partners. The Department of Business Administration is a large and diverse unit, which includes graduate and undergraduate programs across seven academic areas (i.e., Organizational Behavior, Strategic Management, International Business, Marketing, Operations Management, Information Systems, and Supply Chain). We offer a uniquely hospitable environment for interdisciplinary work, as well as the opportunity to work with talented doctoral students. We seek individuals who are committed to engaged scholarship of the highest caliber. Additional information about the Department may be found here . SPECIFIC DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES Maintain an active and productive program of research Teach at the graduate and undergraduate levels. Perform service for the department. Provide leadership in the department and the university. MINIMUM QUALIFICATIONS Candidates for assistant professor should expect to have completed their doctoral degree by June 1, 2027 Strong research portfolio Demonstrated teaching effectiveness Leadership potential commensurate with position sought SALARY AND APPOINTMENT INFORMATION This is a 9-month, 100%-time academic tenure-track position with the opportunity for summer appointment. The expected start date is August 16, 2027 or January 1, 2028. The budgeted salary range for this position is $200,000-$220,000 at the Assistant Professor level or $210,000-$240,000 at the Associate Professor level, and $230,000-$280,000 at the Professor level The pay offered to the selected candidate will be determined based on factors including (but not limited to) the experience and qualifications of the selected candidate including equivalent years in rank, training, and field or discipline; internal equity; and external market pay for comparable jobs. This position is eligible for visa sponsorship except for sponsorship of a new H1B petition that would incur the $100,000 fee. APPLICATION PROCEDURES & DEADLINE INFORMATION For full consideration, please submit a cover letter, curriculum vitae, contact information of three professional references, and evidence of past teaching success. Applications must be received by 6:00 pm (Central Time) on December 20, 2026 . Apply for this position using the Apply Now button at the top or bottom of this posting. Interviews may occur prior to the initial closing date; however, the review of applications will continue until suitable candidates are identified. Applications not submitted through https://jobs.illinois.edu will not be considered. For further information about this specific position, please contact Stephanie Overmier at business-bahr@business .. For questions regarding the application process, please contact 217-333-2137. Founded in 1867 as Illinois’s flagship public university, the University of Illinois Urbana-Champaign empowers a global community of students, scholars, and alumni to change the world through bold, innovative research and transformative education. With a land-grant heritage rooted in progress, Illinois faculty drive paradigm-shifting discoveries, mentor future leaders, and collaborate across 15 colleges and instructional units and more than 20 research institutes. The university’s legacy of excellence includes 24 Nobel Prizes and 29 Pulitzer Prizes awarded to its faculty and alumni, $755 million in sponsored research funding, and 94 academic programs ranked in the top 20 nationally. Illinois offers the resources, recognition, and reach to accelerate your career — along with a highly competitive benefits portfolio. Discover how the Illinois Value Proposition fosters professional longevity, personal fulfillment, and a deep sense of purpose in every role. Faculty Recruitment Champaign-Urbana Artificial Intelligence (AI) tools may be used in some portions of the candidate review process for this position; however, all employment decisions will be made by a person. This position is intended to be eligible for benefits . This includes Health, Dental, Vision, Life Insurance, a Retirement Plan, Paid time Off, and Tuition waivers for employees and dependents. The University of Illinois System is an equal opportunity employer, including but not limited to disability and/or veteran status, and complies with all applicable state and federal employment mandates. Please visit Required Employment Notices and Posters to view our non-discrimination statement and find additional information about required background checks, sexual harassment/misconduct disclosures, and employment eligibility review through E-Verify . Applicants with disabilities are encouraged to apply and may request a reasonable accommodation under the Americans with Disabilities Act (2008) to complete the application and/or interview process. Accommodations may also be requested on the basis of pregnancy, childbirth, and related conditions, or religion. Requests may be submitted through the reasonable accommodation portal , or by contacting the Office for Access & Equity at 217-333-0885, option #1, or accessibility@illinois.edu . Requisition ID : 1037877 Job Category : Faculty Apply at: https://jobs.illinois.edu Apply Now Share Save Job Looking for more University of Illinois Positions? We invite you to search for positions at each of the University of Illinois' locations, the University of Illinois System Office and the University of Illinois Foundation. The University of Illinois System Office supports the primary missions of teaching, research, public service, and economic development for all of the Universities and offers positions in all locations. The University of Illinois Foundation is the official fundraising and private gift-receiving agency for the University of Illinois and also offers position in all locations.  Click the links below to search for other University of Illinois positions. University of Illinois Chicago University of Illinois Springfield University of Illinois System Office University of Illinois Foundation Illinois Human Resources University of Illinois Urbana-Champaign Personnel Services Building - MC 562 52 E. Gregory Dr. Champaign, IL  61820 217.333.2137 | jobs@illinois.edu humanresources.illinois.edu"
